rom rat bone marrow cell cultures</article-title><source>J Pineal Res</source><year>1992</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1578339</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-079X.1992.tb00030.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marco</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosero</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Villa</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Esquifino</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Larralde</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of p-chlorophenylalanine on LH, FSH, prolactin and ovulation in the rat</article-title><source>Rev Esp Fisiol</source><year>1982</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6218542</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Steinman</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlton</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Haber</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential effects of p-chlorophenylalanine on indoleamines in brainstem nuclei and spinal cord of rats. I. Biochemical and behavioral analysis</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1987</year><volume>426</volume><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>309</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2446710</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0006-8993(87)90883-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramachandran</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pa