ts selected for reduced aggressiveness toward humans</article-title><source>Comp Biochem Physiol C Toxicol Pharmacol</source><year>2000</year><volume>125</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11790329</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Butkevich</surname><given-names>IP</given-names></name><name><surname>Khozhai</surname><given-names>LI</given-names></name><name><surname>Mikhailenko</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Otellin</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decreased serotonin level during pregnancy alters morphological and functional characteristics of tonic nociceptive system in juvenile offspring of the rat</article-title><source>Reprod Biol Endocrinol</source><year>2003</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>96</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14614772</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1477-7827-1-96</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maestroni</surname><given-names>GJM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pierpaoli</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ader R</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Pharmacologic control of the hormonall mediated immune response</article-title><source>Psychoneuroimmunology</source><year>1981</year><publisher-name>Academic Press, New York</publisher-name><fpage>405</fpage><lpage>425</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Demas</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kriegsfeld</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><